{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs GNU C++17 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following GNU C++17 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nIntegers from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ (inclusive) were sorted lexicographically (considering integers as strings). As a result, array $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n$$$ was obtained.Calculate value of $$$(\\sum_{i = 1}^n ((i - a_i) \\mod 998244353)) \\mod 10^9 + 7$$$.$$$x \\mod y$$$ here means the remainder after division $$$x$$$ by $$$y$$$. This remainder is always non-negative and doesn't exceed $$$y - 1$$$. For example, $$$5 \\mod 3 = 2$$$, $$$(-1) \\mod 6 = 5$$$. \n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the GNU C++17 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <random>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <functional>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i64 = long long;\nusing i32 = int;\n\nconst i64 MOD = 1000000007;\nconst i64 MOD2 = 998244353;\n\nmt19937_64 rng(random_device{}());\n\nvector<int> pos[7];\ni64 s[7];\ni64 cnt2;\ni64 n;\ni32 ans;\n\ninline i64 modPow(i64 a, i64 b) {\n    i64 res = 1;\n    a %= MOD;\n    while (b) {\n        if (b & 1) res = (res * a) % MOD;\n        a = (a * a) % MOD;\n        b >>= 1;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\ninline i64 modAdd(i64 a, i64 b) {\n    return ((a % MOD) + (b % MOD)) % MOD;\n}\n\ninline i64 modMul(i64 a, i64 b) {\n    return ((a % MOD) * (b % MOD)) % MOD;\n}\n\ni32 queryFixedPrefix(i64 fixpre, i64 val) {\n    i64 res = 0;\n    for (int d = 0; d < 7; ++d) {\n        i64 offset = (val - fixpre * modPow(10, d)) % MOD2;\n        if (offset < 0) offset += MOD2;\n        auto lb = lower_bound(pos[d].begin(), pos[d].end(), MOD2 - offset);\n        int p = lb - pos[d].begin();\n        i64 sz = pos[d].size();\n        i64 term = modAdd(modAdd(res, s[d]), modMul(offset, sz));\n        term = modAdd(term, MOD2 * (sz - p));\n        res = term % MOD;\n    }\n    return (i32)res;\n}\n\nvoid buildPos(i64 val, int d) {\n    i64 x = ((cnt2 - val) % MOD2 + MOD2) % MOD2;\n    pos[d].push_back((int)x);\n    cnt2++;\n    s[d] = modAdd(s[d], x);\n    if (d == 6) return;\n    for (int i = 0; i < 10; ++i) {\n        buildPos(val * 10 + i, d + 1);\n    }\n}\n\nvoid countNumbers(i64 val) {\n    i64 low = val * 1000000 + 999999;\n    i64 high = val * 10000000;\n    if (low <= n && high > n) {\n        ans = modAdd(ans, queryFixedPrefix(val, cnt2 + 1));\n        i64 total = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < 7; ++i) total += pos[i].size();\n        cnt2 += total;\n    } else {\n        cnt2++;\n        i64 diff = ((cnt2 - val) % MOD2 + MOD2) % MOD2;\n        ans = modAdd(ans, diff);\n        for (int i = (val ? 0 : 1); i < 10; ++i) {\n            i64 nextVal = val * 10 + i;\n            if (nextVal <= n) {\n                countNumbers(nextVal);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    buildPos(0, 0);\n    for (int i = 0; i < 7; ++i) {\n        sort(pos[i].begin(), pos[i].end());\n    }\n    \n    cin >> n;\n    cnt2 = -1;\n    countNumbers(0);\n    cout << ans << '\\n';\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cmath>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i64 = long long;\n\nconst i64 MOD = 1000000007;\nconst i64 MOD2 = 998244353;\n\ni64 n;\ni64 total = 0;\ni64 sum_diff = 0;\n\n// Calculate the lexicographic rank of number x among numbers 1..n\ni64 getLexRank(i64 x) {\n    i64 rank = 1;\n    for (i64 i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n        string a = to_string(i);\n        string b = to_string(x);\n        if (a < b) rank++;\n        else if (a == b) break;\n    }\n    return rank;\n}\n\n// Calculate sum of (i - a_i) mod 998244353 for i=1..n, then mod 10^9+7\ni64 solve() {\n    i64 result = 0;\n    for (i64 i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n        string s = to_string(i);\n        // Generate all numbers from 1 to n and sort lexicographically\n    }\n    \n    // Create array of pairs (string representation, original number)\n    vector<pair<string, i64>> nums;\n    for (i64 i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n        nums.push_back({to_string(i), i});\n    }\n    \n    // Sort lexicographically\n    sort(nums.begin(), nums.end());\n    \n    // Calculate the sum\n    for (i64 i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        i64 a_i = nums[i].second;\n        i64 diff = (i + 1 - a_i) % MOD2;\n        if (diff < 0) diff += MOD2;\n        result = (result + diff) % MOD;\n    }\n    \n    return result;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    cin >> n;\n    cout << solve() << '\\n';\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.3\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.1920922133867862e-06, -2.7179348762729205e-05, -3.814689989667386e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -8.22540732769994e-06, 0.0, -0.00010942813969450071, 0.0, -0.00011312322021694854, 0.0, -4.291525328881107e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -9.536697689327411e-06, 0.0, -2.682172998902388e-05, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -0.07890483736991882, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0011044599814340472,